WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.395
Lesson 5.6.

00:00:02.395 --> 00:00:06.723
Beyond Ethereum: Solana, Bitcoin and other ecosystems.

00:00:06.723 --> 00:00:09.100
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.992
able to operate safely on non-EVM chains and

00:00:11.992 --> 00:00:14.498
understand how Bitcoin is used in DeFi.

00:00:15.798 --> 00:00:17.088
Here's the plan.

00:00:17.088 --> 00:00:18.773
First, the key ideas.

00:00:18.773 --> 00:00:21.488
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.013
Then, your checklist.

00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:25.175
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:26.476 --> 00:00:30.242
First, Solana: a separate, high-throughput chain with

00:00:30.242 --> 00:00:33.451
its own wallets (e.g. Phantom, Solflare), its

00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:36.240
own address format, very low fees (paid

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.121
in SOL), and priority fees when busy.

00:00:39.121 --> 00:00:41.991
Tokens follow its own standard (SPL).

00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:44.406
Your Ethereum address doesn't work there.

00:00:44.406 --> 00:00:48.306
Sending between ecosystems needs a bridge or an exchange.

00:00:48.306 --> 00:00:51.516
Next, Bitcoin in DeFi: BTC itself doesn't run

00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:54.098
DeFi apps, so it's usually used as a

00:00:54.098 --> 00:00:57.099
wrapped token on other chains (backed by a

00:00:57.099 --> 00:01:00.379
custodian, a group of signers, or a protocol),

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:03.331
or on Bitcoin layer 2s and sidechains.

00:01:03.331 --> 00:01:05.721
Each wrapper has its own trust model.

00:01:05.721 --> 00:01:07.476
Your "BTC" is only as good

00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:09.726
as whoever holds the real BTC.

00:01:09.726 --> 00:01:13.798
Then, Other ecosystems (e.g. Cosmos chains connected

00:01:13.798 --> 00:01:17.101
by IBC, Move-based chains) each have their

00:01:17.101 --> 00:01:19.706
own wallets, fees and bridges.

00:01:19.706 --> 00:01:22.596
Apply Module 5's dependency map to each.

00:01:22.596 --> 00:01:25.949
And finally, Same rules everywhere: official wallet

00:01:25.949 --> 00:01:29.044
from the official site, test transaction first,

00:01:29.044 --> 00:01:31.301
correct network, gas token on hand.

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:35.116
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:35.116 --> 00:01:36.712
You hold 1 BTC and want

00:01:36.712 --> 00:01:38.541
to lend it on Ethereum.

00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:41.812
Options: a custodial wrapper (trust one company),

00:01:41.812 --> 00:01:44.690
a decentralised wrapper (trust a signer set

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.411
or protocol), or not wrapping at all.

00:01:47.411 --> 00:01:50.282
Write each option's trust model and cap

00:01:50.282 --> 00:01:52.651
wrapped BTC as bridge risk (5.1).

00:01:53.951 --> 00:01:55.411
Here's your checklist.

00:01:55.411 --> 00:01:56.946
Do it now, for real.

00:01:56.946 --> 00:01:59.348
First, Separate, official wallet for

00:01:59.348 --> 00:02:01.271
each non-EVM chain I use.

00:02:01.271 --> 00:02:03.766
Next, Gas token held on each chain.

00:02:03.766 --> 00:02:07.030
And finally, Wrapped-BTC trust model known and capped.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.540
Question 1.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.875
Does your Ethereum address work on Solana?

00:02:16.295 --> 00:02:18.951
The answer: No. It's a different ecosystem

00:02:18.951 --> 00:02:21.421
with its own address format and wallets.

00:02:22.721 --> 00:02:23.966
Question 2.

00:02:23.966 --> 00:02:26.441
What determines a wrapped BTC token's safety?

00:02:30.861 --> 00:02:33.366
The answer: Who holds the real BTC and

00:02:33.366 --> 00:02:35.936
how it can be redeemed: its trust model.

00:02:37.236 --> 00:02:38.506
Question 3.

00:02:38.506 --> 00:02:40.061
What's Solana's gas token?

00:02:44.481 --> 00:02:45.736
The answer: SOL.

00:02:47.036 --> 00:02:48.281
Let's recap.

00:02:48.281 --> 00:02:51.267
Solana: a separate, high-throughput chain with

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:54.171
its own wallets (e.g. Phantom, Solflare).

00:02:54.171 --> 00:02:58.076
Bitcoin in DeFi: BTC itself doesn't run DeFi apps.

00:02:58.076 --> 00:03:03.266
Other ecosystems (e.g. Cosmos chains connected by IBC.

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:05.932
Same rules everywhere: official wallet from

00:03:05.932 --> 00:03:08.476
the official site, test transaction first.

00:03:09.776 --> 00:03:12.291
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.305
Next up, Lesson 5.7: Operating across

00:03:15.305 --> 00:03:18.636
chains: gas, routes and chain abstraction.
